'Cannabis is prohibited in Kosovo under the Law on Prevention of and Fight against Narcotic Drugs. Kosovo, a partially recognized state, has been working to align its legal framework with EU standards as part of its EU integration aspirations. There is no medical cannabis program. Enforcement capacity is developing as Kosovo strengthens its institutions.',
'No legal patient access exists. Cannabis-based medicines are unavailable through official Kosovar healthcare channels.',
'Kosovar physicians cannot prescribe cannabis under the existing legal framework.',
'No licensed cannabis market exists. Kosovo''s geographic position in the Western Balkans creates some cross-border informal trade dynamics.',
'EU integration aspirations may eventually drive alignment with EU medical cannabis norms. No imminent legislative action is anticipated.',
'Kosovo Police handles drug enforcement. Ministry of Health oversees pharmaceutical regulation.',
'Kosovo Law on Prevention of Narcotic Drugs; Ministry of Health pharmaceutical policy; EU integration monitoring','Current as of Q2 2026','Annual','Country-level briefing noting prohibition with EU integration policy context',DATE '2026-06-21','[]'::jsonb,'[]'::jsonb,'reviewed'
