SELECT 'latvia','country','LV','Medical Legal (Limited); CBD Regulated',
'Latvia established a limited medical cannabis framework under pharmaceutical regulations, permitting access to cannabis-based medicines on a named-patient basis. Latvia has also implemented one of the EU''s clearer regulatory frameworks for CBD products, treating them as novel foods under EU Novel Foods Regulation. Recreational use remains prohibited with criminal penalties.',
'Patients may access cannabis-based medicines through named-patient authorization from the State Agency of Medicines with physician prescription. Products must be pharmacy-dispensed. Patient numbers are limited due to administrative requirements.',
'Latvian physicians may apply for named-patient authorization to prescribe cannabis-based medicines. The process involves regulatory approval and is administratively demanding. No domestic production exists.',
'Latvia''s medical cannabis market is very small. The CBD consumer goods market operates under the EU Novel Foods framework. International cannabis companies supply Latvian named-patient prescriptions through import authorizations.',
'Latvia may develop a broader medical cannabis program as EU harmonization progresses. CBD regulatory clarity provides a positive foundation for expanded cannabis product frameworks.',
'State Agency of Medicines (Zāļu valsts aģentūra/ZVA) regulates medical cannabis products and authorizations. Ministry of Health sets health policy.',
'ZVA pharmaceutical registry and authorization data; Latvia Novel Foods CBD framework; EMCDDA Latvia report','Current as of Q2 2026; verified against ZVA official guidance','Annual','Country-level briefing covering limited medical access and regulated CBD framework',DATE '2026-06-21','[]'::jsonb,'[]'::jsonb,'reviewed'
