SELECT 'liechtenstein','country','LI','Prohibited; Swiss Framework Adjacent',
'Cannabis is prohibited in Liechtenstein under the Betäubungsmittelgesetz (Narcotics Act). Liechtenstein closely aligns its legal framework with Switzerland given its customs union and economic integration. Switzerland has enacted adult-use pilot programs, but Liechtenstein has not followed with equivalent legislation. There is no medical cannabis program.',
'No formal patient access exists in Liechtenstein. Residents may potentially access Swiss medical cannabis systems given cross-border integration, but no domestic framework exists.',
'Liechtenstein physicians cannot prescribe cannabis domestically. Cross-border access to Swiss medical frameworks may be practically available to some residents.',
'No licensed cannabis market exists in Liechtenstein. Swiss cannabis developments may have indirect influence given economic integration.',
'Liechtenstein may follow Switzerland''s evolution if the Swiss adult-use pilot programs lead to full legalization, but no independent legislative action is expected.',
'Liechtenstein National Police handles drug enforcement. Office for Health handles pharmaceutical regulation.',
'Liechtenstein Betäubungsmittelgesetz; Swiss-Liechtenstein customs union arrangements; EMCDDA monitoring','Current as of Q2 2026','Annual','Country-level briefing noting prohibition with Swiss framework adjacency',DATE '2026-06-21','[]'::jsonb,'[]'::jsonb,'reviewed'
