SELECT 'lithuania','country','LT','Medical Legal',
'Lithuania established a medical cannabis framework through the Law on Narcotic and Psychotropic Substances amendments in 2018. The program allows physician prescription of medical cannabis products for qualifying conditions. Lithuania has taken a measured but functional approach to medical access, distinguishing it from some Baltic peers.',
'Patients access medical cannabis through licensed pharmacies with physician prescription. Products include approved cannabis-based medicines available through import authorization. Patient registration is not required. Out-of-pocket costs apply as health insurance reimbursement is limited.',
'Lithuanian physicians may prescribe medical cannabis for conditions including multiple sclerosis, chronic pain, and chemotherapy-related symptoms. No specialist-only restriction applies in general, though complex conditions typically involve specialist input.',
'Lithuania''s medical cannabis market is small but functional. Products are supplied through import authorization pathways. Domestic cultivation has not been licensed for medical purposes, though industrial hemp is grown commercially.',
'Lithuania may develop domestic medical cannabis production as EU harmonization creates market opportunities. Further program expansion is expected as clinical evidence accumulates.',
'State Medicines Control Agency (SMCA/Valstybinė vaistų kontrolės agentūra) regulates medical cannabis products. Ministry of Health sets clinical guidelines.',
'SMCA pharmaceutical registry; Lithuanian Law on Narcotic and Psychotropic Substances 2018 amendment; EMCDDA Lithuania report','Current as of Q2 2026','Annual','Country-level briefing covering functional medical cannabis program',DATE '2026-06-21','[]'::jsonb,'[]'::jsonb,'reviewed'
