SELECT 'north-macedonia','country','MK','Medical Legal',
'North Macedonia introduced a medical cannabis framework in 2016 through amendments to the Law on Psychotropic Substances. The program permits licensed cultivation, processing, and prescription of medical cannabis products. North Macedonia has also developed an export-oriented licensed cannabis cultivation sector targeting EU markets, taking advantage of its climate and lower production costs relative to Western Europe.',
'Patients access medical cannabis through licensed pharmacies with physician prescription. Both domestically produced and imported products are available. Patient registration is required. Limited health insurance coverage exists for specific conditions.',
'Macedonian physicians may prescribe medical cannabis for qualifying conditions including epilepsy, multiple sclerosis, and chronic pain. Specialist recommendation may be required for initial prescriptions.',
'North Macedonia has developed a licensed medical cannabis production sector with export orientation. Several international cannabis companies have established Macedonian growing operations. The export market, primarily targeting Germany and other EU markets, represents a significant economic opportunity.',
'North Macedonia''s medical cannabis sector is expected to continue growing, particularly export capacity. EU accession aspirations may drive further regulatory harmonization. The country''s production cost advantages position it competitively in European supply chains.',
'Agency for Drugs and Medical Devices (MALMED) regulates medical cannabis. Ministry of Agriculture oversees cultivation licensing.',
'North Macedonia Law on Psychotropic Substances 2016; MALMED regulatory guidance; Ministry of Agriculture cultivation license data; EU accession monitoring','Current as of Q2 2026','Quarterly','Country-level briefing covering medical program and export-oriented cultivation sector',DATE '2026-06-21','[]'::jsonb,'[]'::jsonb,'reviewed'
